          "id": "MYS-MALACCA",
          "text": "Malacca Sultanate and port administration · 15th century; Atlas context approximately 1400–1511\n\nThe Customs Department’s historical publication describes Syahbandar assigned to merchant groups, with duties covering markets, warehouses, measures, ship movements and taxation. It supports a port-administration account, not a complete annual tariff or individual transaction ledger.\n\nHistorical Melaka port and visiting merchants; present-day Melaka is a place cross-reference\n\nRoyal Malaysian Customs · Menelusuri Susur Galur Syahbandar (2022)\n\nRelated Atlas interpretation: Malacca Sultanate\n\nSource and scope",
          "sources": [
            "https://www.customs.gov.my/images/penerbitan/syahbandar-2022.pdf"
          ]
        }
